BDSIM build environment Dockerfiles
----------------------------------

All environment dockerfiles have now moved to a separate repo `bdsim-collaboration docker<https://github.com/bdsim-collaboration/docker>`_
and are available in dockerhub `bdsim docker team <https://hub.docker.com/u/bdsim>`_

If you wish to check the files that were stored here: :: 

   git checkout develop
   git checkout 84f07ca71293621fc13070f54e8117e0c9b5f019


Docker build environments for Testing
-------------------------------------

Docker images exist with the software environment to build BDSIM (i.e CLHEP, Geant4 etc). These are all available from
dockerhub and are used to perform our testing of BDSIM.

Command to get a given image: ::

  docker pull bdsim/<IMAGENAME> 

Command to run a given image: ::

  docker run -ti bdsim/<IMAGENAME>


Buiding docker BDSIM
--------------------

The dockerfiles here are for building docker images that contain an operating version of BDSIM. These images
are based on the testing images. In generate you are welcome to use them and adapt the dockerfiles, but the
primary aim of these dockerfiles/images is to perform regression testing in the CI/CD (GitHub)

To build a BDSIM docker image: ::

   docker build -t <YOUR_TAG> -f <DOCKERFILE> <CONTEXT>

So for example to build alma9 Geant4.11.3 with develop BDSIM

   docker build -t alma9-g4.11.3-bdsim -f alma9-g4.11.3-bdsim .
   
